    {"id": "bene", "tr": {}, "exams": ["ssc", "bank"], "term": "bene", "forms": ["beni"], "origin": "Latin", "unit": "Good, bad and judgement", "en": "good, well", "bn": "ভালো", "hi": "अच्छा", "note": "Bene means good or well. Put it at the start of a word and the word usually describes something kind or helpful.", "words": [{"word": "benefit", "en": "An advantage", "bn": "সুবিধা", "hi": "लाभ"}, {"word": "benevolent", "en": "Kind and generous", "bn": "পরোপকারী", "hi": "परोपकारी"}, {"word": "benefactor", "en": "A person who gives help or money", "bn": "পৃষ্ঠপোষক", "hi": "संरक्षक"}, {"word": "beneficiary", "en": "A person who receives a benefit", "bn": "সুবিধাভোগী", "hi": "लाभार्थी"}, {"word": "benign", "en": "Gentle and harmless", "bn": "নিরীহ", "hi": "सौम्य"}, {"word": "benediction", "en": "A blessing", "bn": "আশীর্বাদ", "hi": "आशीर्वाद"}], "ex": "A benevolent trader paid the fees of poor students."},
    {"id": "mal", "tr": {}, "exams": ["ssc", "bank"], "term": "mal", "forms": ["male"], "origin": "Latin", "unit": "Good, bad and judgement", "en": "bad, badly", "bn": "মন্দ", "hi": "बुरा", "note": "Mal means bad. It is the opposite of bene, so many mal- words pair with a bene- word.", "words": [{"word": "malevolent", "en": "Wishing harm to others", "bn": "বিদ্বেষপরায়ণ", "hi": "द्वेषपूर्ण"}, {"word": "malice", "en": "The wish to harm", "bn": "বিদ্বেষ", "hi": "द्वेष"}, {"word": "malnutrition", "en": "Poor nutrition", "bn": "অপুষ্টি", "hi": "कुपोषण"}, {"word": "malfunction", "en": "Fail to work properly", "bn": "বিকল হওয়া", "hi": "खराबी"}, {"word": "malign", "en": "Speak badly of", "bn": "নিন্দা করা", "hi": "बदनाम करना"}, {"word": "malpractice", "en": "Wrong or careless professional conduct", "bn": "অসদাচরণ", "hi": "कदाचार"}], "ex": "Malnutrition remains a challenge in many districts."},
    {"id": "chron", "tr": {}, "exams": ["ssc", "bank"], "term": "chron", "forms": [], "origin": "Greek", "unit": "Time and place", "en": "time", "bn": "সময়", "hi": "समय", "note": "Chronos was the Greek word for time. Words with chron are about time, order in time, or lasting a long time.", "words": [{"word": "chronic", "en": "Lasting a long time", "bn": "দীর্ঘস্থায়ী", "hi": "दीर्घकालिक"}, {"word": "chronology", "en": "The order in which events happened", "bn": "কালানুক্রম", "hi": "कालक्रम"}, {"word": "chronicle", "en": "A record of events in order", "bn": "ইতিবৃত্ত", "hi": "इतिवृत्त"}, {"word": "synchronise", "en": "Make things happen at the same time", "bn": "একই সময়ে মেলানো", "hi": "समकालिक करना"}, {"word": "anachronism", "en": "Something out of its proper time", "bn": "কালবিরুদ্ধ বস্তু", "hi": "कालदोष"}], "ex": "The history notes follow a strict chronology."},
    {"id": "loqu", "tr": {}, "exams": ["ssc", "bank"], "term": "loqu", "forms": ["locu"], "origin": "Latin", "unit": "Speaking and writing", "en": "speak, talk", "bn": "কথা বলা", "hi": "बोलना", "note": "Loqu (also locu) means to speak. These words describe how, how much or how well someone talks.", "words": [{"word": "eloquent", "en": "Speaking fluently and persuasively", "bn": "বাগ্মী", "hi": "वाक्पटु"}, {"word": "loquacious", "en": "Talking a lot", "bn": "বাচাল", "hi": "बातूनी"}, {"word": "soliloquy", "en": "A speech to oneself", "bn": "স্বগতোক্তি", "hi": "स्वगत भाषण"}, {"word": "colloquial", "en": "Used in everyday talk", "bn": "কথ্য", "hi": "बोलचाल का"}, {"word": "circumlocution", "en": "Using many words to avoid saying something directly", "bn": "ঘুরিয়ে বলা", "hi": "घुमा-फिराकर बात"}], "ex": "The loquacious guide talked for the whole journey."},
    {"id": "bio", "tr": {}, "exams": ["ssc", "bank"], "term": "bio", "forms": [], "origin": "Greek", "unit": "Life, body and nature", "en": "life", "bn": "জীবন", "hi": "जीवन", "note": "Bio means life. It appears in science words and in words about a person's life story.", "words": [{"word": "biology", "en": "The study of living things", "bn": "জীববিদ্যা", "hi": "जीव विज्ञान"}, {"word": "biography", "en": "The story of someone's life", "bn": "জীবনী", "hi": "जीवनी"}, {"word": "antibiotic", "en": "A medicine that kills bacteria", "bn": "জীবাণুনাশক ওষুধ", "hi": "प्रतिजैविक"}, {"word": "biodiversity", "en": "The variety of life in an area", "bn": "জীববৈচিত্র্য", "hi": "जैव विविधता"}, {"word": "symbiosis", "en": "Two living things helping each other", "bn": "মিথোজীবিতা", "hi": "सहजीवन"}], "ex": "The Western Ghats are rich in biodiversity."},
    {"id": "phil", "tr": {}, "exams": ["ssc", "bank"], "term": "phil", "forms": ["phile"], "origin": "Greek", "unit": "Mind and feelings", "en": "love", "bn": "ভালোবাসা", "hi": "प्रेम", "note": "Phil means love. At the start of a word it means love of something; as -phile at the end it means a lover of something.", "words": [{"word": "philanthropy", "en": "Love of people shown by helping them", "bn": "জনহিতৈষণা", "hi": "परोपकार"}, {"word": "philosophy", "en": "The love and study of wisdom", "bn": "দর্শন", "hi": "दर्शन"}, {"word": "bibliophile", "en": "A lover of books", "bn": "গ্রন্থপ্রেমী", "hi": "पुस्तक-प्रेमी"}, {"word": "philately", "en": "Stamp collecting", "bn": "ডাকটিকিট সংগ্রহ", "hi": "डाक-टिकट संग्रह"}, {"word": "anglophile", "en": "A lover of English culture", "bn": "ইংরেজপ্রেমী", "hi": "अंग्रेज़-प्रेमी"}], "ex": "Her philanthropy built a school in the village."},
    {"id": "vert", "tr": {}, "exams": ["ssc", "bank"], "term": "vert", "forms": ["vers"], "origin": "Latin", "unit": "Actions and movement", "en": "turn", "bn": "ঘোরানো", "hi": "मोड़ना", "note": "Vert (also vers) means to turn. These words are about turning, changing direction or changing form.", "words": [{"word": "convert", "en": "Change into something else", "bn": "রূপান্তর করা", "hi": "बदलना"}, {"word": "divert", "en": "Turn aside", "bn": "অন্যদিকে ঘোরানো", "hi": "मोड़ना"}, {"word": "introvert", "en": "A person turned inward", "bn": "অন্তর্মুখী", "hi": "अंतर्मुखी"}, {"word": "reverse", "en": "Turn back", "bn": "উল্টানো", "hi": "उलटना"}, {"word": "versatile", "en": "Able to turn to many tasks", "bn": "বহুমুখী", "hi": "बहुमुखी"}, {"word": "avert", "en": "Turn away or prevent", "bn": "এড়ানো", "hi": "टालना"}], "ex": "Quick action helped avert a disaster."},
    {"id": "omni", "tr": {}, "exams": ["ssc", "bank"], "term": "omni", "forms": [], "origin": "Latin", "unit": "Size, number and amount", "en": "all", "bn": "সব", "hi": "सब", "note": "Omni means all. Add it to a word and the meaning stretches to everything or everywhere.", "words": [{"word": "omnipotent", "en": "All-powerful", "bn": "সর্বশক্তিমান", "hi": "सर्वशक्तिमान"}, {"word": "omniscient", "en": "All-knowing", "bn": "সর্বজ্ঞ", "hi": "सर्वज्ञ"}, {"word": "omnipresent", "en": "Present everywhere", "bn": "সর্বব্যাপী", "hi": "सर्वव्यापी"}, {"word": "omnivore", "en": "An animal that eats everything", "bn": "সর্বভুক", "hi": "सर्वाहारी"}], "ex": "Smartphones seem omnipresent today."},
    {"id": "cred", "tr": {}, "exams": ["ssc", "bank"], "term": "cred", "forms": [], "origin": "Latin", "unit": "Seeing, hearing and knowing", "en": "believe, trust", "bn": "বিশ্বাস", "hi": "विश्वास", "note": "Cred means to believe. These words are about trust, belief and whether something can be believed.", "words": [{"word": "credible", "en": "Able to be believed", "bn": "বিশ্বাসযোগ্য", "hi": "विश्वसनीय"}, {"word": "credulous", "en": "Too ready to believe", "bn": "সহজে বিশ্বাসপ্রবণ", "hi": "भोला"}, {"word": "incredible", "en": "Hard to believe", "bn": "অবিশ্বাস্য", "hi": "अविश्वसनीय"}, {"word": "credentials", "en": "Proof of qualifications", "bn": "পরিচয়পত্র", "hi": "प्रमाण-पत्र"}, {"word": "discredit", "en": "Make others stop trusting", "bn": "অবিশ্বাস্য প্রমাণ করা", "hi": "बदनाम करना"}], "ex": "The witness gave a credible account."},
    {"id": "dict", "tr": {}, "exams": ["ssc", "bank"], "term": "dict", "forms": ["dic"], "origin": "Latin", "unit": "Speaking and writing", "en": "say, tell", "bn": "বলা", "hi": "कहना", "note": "Dict means to say. These words are about saying, ordering or judging with words.", "words": [{"word": "dictate", "en": "Say aloud for someone to write", "bn": "বলে লেখানো", "hi": "लिखवाना"}, {"word": "predict", "en": "Say what will happen", "bn": "ভবিষ্যদ্বাণী করা", "hi": "भविष्यवाणी करना"}, {"word": "contradict", "en": "Say the opposite", "bn": "খণ্ডন করা", "hi": "खंडन करना"}, {"word": "verdict", "en": "A judgement", "bn": "রায়", "hi": "फ़ैसला"}, {"word": "diction", "en": "The way words are chosen and spoken", "bn": "উচ্চারণভঙ্গি", "hi": "उच्चारण शैली"}, {"word": "edict", "en": "An official order", "bn": "রাজাজ্ঞা", "hi": "राजाज्ञा"}], "ex": "Experts predict heavy rain this week."},
    {"id": "spect", "tr": {}, "exams": ["ssc", "bank"], "term": "spect", "forms": ["spic"], "origin": "Latin", "unit": "Seeing, hearing and knowing", "en": "look, see", "bn": "দেখা", "hi": "देखना", "note": "Spect (also spic) means to look. These words are about watching, examining or a way of seeing.", "words": [{"word": "inspect", "en": "Look at closely", "bn": "পরিদর্শন করা", "hi": "निरीक्षण करना"}, {"word": "spectator", "en": "A person who watches", "bn": "দর্শক", "hi": "दर्शक"}, {"word": "retrospect", "en": "Looking back", "bn": "পিছনে ফিরে দেখা", "hi": "पुनरावलोकन"}, {"word": "circumspect", "en": "Careful, looking all around", "bn": "সতর্ক", "hi": "सतर्क"}, {"word": "conspicuous", "en": "Easy to see", "bn": "সুস্পষ্ট", "hi": "स्पष्ट"}, {"word": "perspective", "en": "A way of seeing things", "bn": "দৃষ্টিভঙ্গি", "hi": "दृष्टिकोण"}], "ex": "Officials inspect the bridge every year."},
    {"id": "greg", "tr": {}, "exams": ["ssc", "bank"], "term": "greg", "forms": [], "origin": "Latin", "unit": "Society, law and power", "en": "flock, group", "bn": "দল", "hi": "समूह", "note": "Greg means a flock or group. These words are about coming together or being kept apart.", "words": [{"word": "gregarious", "en": "Fond of company", "bn": "মিশুক", "hi": "मिलनसार"}, {"word": "congregate", "en": "Gather together", "bn": "সমবেত হওয়া", "hi": "एकत्र होना"}, {"word": "segregate", "en": "Keep apart", "bn": "আলাদা করা", "hi": "अलग करना"}, {"word": "aggregate", "en": "The total", "bn": "সমষ্টি", "hi": "कुल योग"}], "ex": "Students congregate in the hall before the assembly."}
  ]
}
